.TH parsec-cli-shared-recovery-create 1  "create " 
.SH NAME
parsec\-cli\-shared\-recovery\-create \- create shared recovery
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBparsec\-cli shared\-recovery create\fR [\fB\-\-password\-stdin\fR] [\fB\-d\fR|\fB\-\-device\fR] [\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-config\-dir\fR] [\fB\-\-recipients\fR] [\fB\-t\fR|\fB\-\-threshold\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-confirmation\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
create shared recovery
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-password\-stdin\fR
Read the password from stdin instead of TTY. This flag needs to be explicitly set (it does not have a env var)
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-device\fR \fI<DEVICE>\fR
Device ID
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBPARSEC_DEVICE_ID\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\-dir\fR \fI<CONFIG_DIR>\fR [default: /home/redacted/.config/parsec3/libparsec]
Parsec config directory
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBPARSEC_CONFIG_DIR\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-recipients\fR \fI<RECIPIENTS>...\fR
Share recipients, with their weight. If missing organization\*(Aqs admins will be used instead. Author must not be included as recipient. email or email:weight format is expected (weight defaults to one if not provided)
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-threshold\fR \fI<THRESHOLD>\fR
Threshold number of shares required to proceed with recovery
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-confirmation\fR
Whether to ask for confirmation or not
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
